ParentVault_initiateRebalance
├── when the caller does not have REBALANCE_OPERATOR_ROLE
│   └── it should revert
├── when the vault is paused
│   └── it should revert with EnforcedPause
├── when the expected rebalance nonce does not match the current rebalance nonce
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidRebalanceNonce
├── when a rebalance is already in progress
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__RebalanceInProgress
├── when MIN_REBALANCE_PERIOD has not elapsed
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__RebalanceTooSoon
├── when a recovery exists
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
├── when the new strategy is the active strategy
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__SameStrategy
├── when the new strategy chain selector is not supported
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidChainSelector
├── when the new strategy protocol ID is not supported
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidProtocolId
├── when no epochs have completed
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__NoCompletedEpoch
├── when the prior epoch is executing
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__EpochExecuting
├── when the parent rebalances local to local without a crosschain vault self-registration
│   ├── it should withdraw from the old adapter
│   ├── it should deposit into the new adapter
│   ├── it should emit ActiveProtocolAdapterSet
│   └── it should finalize the rebalance
├── when the parent rebalances local to child
│   ├── it should withdraw from the old adapter
│   ├── it should bridge to the child
│   ├── it should emit ActiveProtocolAdapterCleared
│   ├── when the CCIP send reverts
│   │   └── it should revert
│   └── it should leave the rebalance pending
└── when a local adapter operation does not succeed
    ├── when the withdraw reverts
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when withdraw returns 0
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when the deposit reverts
        └── it should revert
